From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Stoffel <stoffel.thomas.ryan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:18:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] telemetry: default the telemetry level to off

wisp's product.json sets enableTelemetry to false and has no telemetry
keys, so a built app never creates a telemetry appender, and extensions
see vscode.env.isTelemetryEnabled as false. The telemetry.telemetryLevel
setting still defaulted to "all", which is what Settings showed.

Default it to "off", so the setting says what the app does, and so
telemetry stays off by default even if a later product.json enabled it.
VSCodium makes the same change in 00-telemetry-disable.patch.

diff --git a/src/vs/platform/telemetry/common/telemetryService.ts b/src/vs/platform/telemetry/common/telemetryService.ts
index 18f60022ff32e28b8126096127f62d935d77f39e..a2263601b7bf44c44b40483c5907b1f5cfe00f15 100644
--- a/src/vs/platform/telemetry/common/telemetryService.ts
+++ b/src/vs/platform/telemetry/common/telemetryService.ts
@@ -328,7 +328,7 @@ configurationRegistry.registerConfiguration({
 				localize('telemetry.telemetryLevel.off', "Disables all product telemetry.")
 			],
 			'markdownDescription': getTelemetryLevelSettingDescription(),
-			'default': TelemetryConfiguration.ON,
+			'default': TelemetryConfiguration.OFF,
 			'restricted': true,
 			'scope': ConfigurationScope.APPLICATION,
 			'tags': ['usesOnlineServices', 'telemetry'],
